{"cuisine/assyrian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/assyrian-cuisine","n":"Assyrian cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"Cuisine of a people","intro":[["Assyrian cuisine is the cuisine of the indigenous Assyrian people, Eastern Aramaic-speaking Syriac Christians of Iraq, northeastern Syria, northwestern Iran and southeastern Turkey. Assyrian cuisine is primarily identical to Iraqi/Mesopotamian cuisine, as well as being very similar to other Middle Eastern and Caucasian cuisines, as well as Greek cuisine, Levantine cuisine, Turkish cuisine, Iranian cuisine, Palestinian cuisine, and Armenian cuisine, with most dishes being similar to the cuisines of the area in which those Assyrians live/originate from. It is rich in grains such as barley, meat, tomato, herbs, spices, and potato as well as fermented dairy products, and pickles."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"assyrian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assyrian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Hilda's Kitchen Blog (Assyrian)","ref":"site/hildaskitchenblog-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"hildaskitchenblog.com","note":"Assyrian home cook Hilda Sterner's blog, with a dedicated Assyrian recipes category.","url":"https://hildaskitchenblog.com/recipe/category/assyrian","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"The Oldest Kitchen in the World","ref":"cookbook/the-oldest-kitchen-in-the-world","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Matay de Mayee","note":"Assyrian recipes and food history from Mesopotamia to the diaspora.","url":"https://www.simonandschuster.net/books/The-Oldest-Kitchen-in-the-World/Matay-de-Mayee/9781962098083","suggested":true}]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"ingredient/mango":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/mango","n":"Mango","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["A mango is an edible stone fruit produced by the tropical tree Mangifera indica. It originated in the area between the northeastern part of the Indian subcontinent and Myanmar. M. indica has been cultivated in South and Southeast Asia since ancient times, resulting in two modern mango cultivar lineages: the \"Indian\" and the \"Southeast Asian\" types. Other species in the genus Mangifera also produce edible fruits called \"mangoes\", most of which are found in the Malesian ecoregion."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-mango"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mango"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Amba (condiment)","dish/amba-condiment"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Mangoes, guavas and mangosteens","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":59195799,"top":[["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",25989479],["Indonesia","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",3909090],["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",3863553],["Pakistan","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine",2570556],["Mexico","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",2533591],["Brazil","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",2205808],["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",1594167],["Bangladesh","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",1593688],["Thailand","cuisine/thai-cuisine",1543500],["Vietnam","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",1433290],["Malawi","cuisine/malawian-cuisine",1321178],["Nigeria","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine",960470],["Kenya","cuisine/kenyan-cuisine",780198],["Philippines","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",761263],["Mali","cuisine/malian-cuisine",732769]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mango pickle","ingredient/mango-pickle"],["Carabao 