sists of a mixture of rice with Bengal gram,, a variety of chickpea, but has several variants with the gram replaced by pigeon peas, or urad beans. In 2018, it was reported that Ahmedabad reportedly had daily consumption of 10,000 kgs of Dhokla."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dhokla"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhokla"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Gujarati cuisine","cuisine/gujarati-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Lentil","ingredient/lentil"],["Mustard oil","ingredient/mustard-oil"],["Sodium bicarbonate","ingredient/sodium-bicarbonate"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spice Up The Curry (Andhra)","ref":"site/spiceupthecurry-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spiceupthecurry.com","note":"Gujarati section of Kanan Patel's Indian vegetarian recipe blog.","url":"https://www.spiceupthecurry.com/category/recipes-by-region/gujarat/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Gujarati cuisine","links":[["Thepla","dish/thepla"],["Undhiyu","dish/undhiyu"]]}]},"ingredient/yomogi":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/yomogi","n":"Yomogi","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Artemisia princeps, also commonly called yomogi, ssuk, Japanese mugwort, Korean wormwood, Korean mugwort or wormwood in English, is an Asian plant species in the sunflower family, native to China, Japan and Korea. It is a perennial, very vigorous plant that grows to 1.2 meters (3 ft 11 in). This species spreads rapidly by means of underground stolons and can become invasive. It bears small, buff-coloured flowers from July to November which are hermaphroditic, and pollinated by wind. The leaves are feather shaped, scalloped and light green, with white dense fuzz on the underside."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-yomogi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yomogi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Kusa mochi","dish/kusa-mochi"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mochi","ingredient/mochi"],["Red bean paste","ingredient/red-bean-paste"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/a/a1/Artemisia_princeps1.jpg","w":500,"h":383,"by":"KENPEI","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artemisia_princeps1.jpg"}},"dish/mexican-restaurants-inc":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mexican-restaurants-inc","n":"Mexican Restaurants, Inc.","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Mexican cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Mexican Restaurants, Inc. is a Houston, Texas-based restaurant company."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mexican-restaurants-inc"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican_Restaurants%2C_Inc."}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","ref":"site/mexicoinmykitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Pati Jinich","ref":"site/patijinich-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Mexican cuisine","links":[["Acapulco Mexican Restaurant and Cantina","dish/acapulco-mexican-restaurant-and-cantina"],["Amigos (restaurant chain)","dish/amigos-restaurant-chain"],["Animalón","dish/animalon"],["Anna's Taqueria","dish/anna-s-taqueria"],["Baker's Drive-Thru","dish/baker-s-drive-thru"],["Barburrito","dish/barburrit